# Text Size Standards

Never use tiny text. All UI text must meet these minimums:

| Role | Min size | Notes |
|------|----------|-------|
| Field labels / caps | 12px | mono, uppercase OK |
| Body / descriptions | 14px | |
| Input values | 15px | |
| Buttons | 14px font-weight 600+ |
| Metric numbers | 20px+ | mono |
| Section headers | 14px font-weight 700 |

❌ BAD — never do this:
```tsx
<p style={{ fontSize: 10 }}>Label</p>
<input style={{ fontSize: 12 }} />
```

✅ GOOD:
```tsx
<p style={{ fontSize: 12, fontFamily:"var(--font-geist-mono)", textTransform:"uppercase", letterSpacing:"0.12em" }}>Label</p>
<input style={{ fontSize: 15, height: 48 }} />
```

- 10px is only acceptable for `<kbd>` shortcut hints or tertiary decorative mono labels
- All interactive elements (buttons, inputs) must be ≥ 14px
- Never shrink text to fit — make the container bigger instead
